# WO-RUST-DOCUMENT-MODEL-01 candidate

Implemented the document model in `rust/crates/vexel-document`: immutable source is borrowed for the model lifetime, while bounded node/attribute tables own tree and live-state metadata. The implementation uses the accepted `XmlTokenStream` 64 MiB actual-capacity contract, preserves tokenizer diagnostics and maps output exhaustion to `ResourceExhausted`. It includes monotonic native atomic IDs, an isolated allocator exhaustion seam, complete element spans, raw names/values, stale-safe handles, tree queries, and subtree removal.

Nine focused tests cover the original C fixture assertions, exact source bytes and spans, attributes, unknown prefixed metadata, comments/DOCTYPE/UTF-8, parse categories and offsets, input/depth/token-storage limits, wrong/stale/deleted handles, removal counts/traversal, error names, and ID exhaustion. The production 64 MiB boundary test reaches the exact original exhaustion diagnostic and offset.

All named checks passed. This is an uncommitted candidate; independent review, preservation audit, and coordinator integration/main checks remain outstanding. No legacy files, XML peer files, manifests, ledgers, or root records were changed. Invalid pointer/length arguments have no Rust equivalent because input is a valid borrowed slice; allocation failures remain fallible.
